  "firstCustomInput": "userTier",
  "firstRuleChain": "",
  "ruleSetPolicy": "",
  "description": "Tier-based access control ensures users have appropriate permissions based on their subscription tier, role, and activity level. This is commonly used in SaaS platforms, membership sites, and enterprise applications.\n\nThe rule engine considers:\n\nUser Tier – Free, Basic, Premium, Enterprise\nUser Role – Viewer, Editor, Admin\nActivity Level – High (Frequent), Medium, Low (Infrequent)\nSpecial Permissions – Whether the user has additional privileges\nThe system dynamically assigns permissions, ensuring security and access control based on user attributes.",
